From 7a7a7663b74c80ea7aa885ec7eaf068eadb997fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vbardales <virginie.bardales@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 23:40:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(input): record image buttons so a click one took
 shows in the report

Pickle records Widgets.ButtonText only, so a Widgets.ButtonImage control
that takes a click leaves no trace and the lost-click report cannot name
it. Postfix every ButtonImage* overload (Harmony) and inject at the tail
of each (Concord), both through one PickleHooks method, and keep the rect
with the other drawn controls. The overloads chain into each other, so a
control reported by several is listed once.

This commit stands apart from the report on purpose: it puts a hook on
widgets Pickle did not touch before. Dropping it leaves the report as it
was, with ButtonText only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
